# -PPA polling is not reliable - they will only go one once the returns processed but they need to wait until the ledger split happens to be confirmed succesful - need to poll a DB somewhere to make sure this has happened before we can pass the test
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  Scenario: 01 Load X amount of payment messages into pay-enrichment

  #Due to call stack limits, 5000 has been determined as the best amount of messages to send in one batch. 
  #This scenario can be re-run multiple times to increase the total number of messages sent however instructions
  #found in Step Definition - 'When I send 5000 payment messages using template "paymentFileMessage" to the service bus topic "ffc-pay-request-auto"'
  #must be followed and the correct code must be commented/uncommented to avoid data duplication

    Given I restart the local environment
    Given I start the messaging service for the service bus topic "ffc-pay-request-dev"
    When I send 300 payment messages using template "paymentFileMessage" to the service bus topic "ffc-pay-request-dev" with the batch number 91000
    Then I wait for 300 payment requests to be ready for settlement for batch 91000
 
  # Scenario: 02 Load X amount of return messages

  # #This scenario repeats the previous process but sends return messages for payment requests generated by Scenario 1

  #   Given I start the messaging service for the service bus topic "ffc-pay-return-dev"
  #   When I send 300 return messages using template "returnFileMessage" to the service bus topic "ffc-pay-return-dev" with the batch number 91000
  #   Then I wait for 300 returns to be processed for batch 91000

  Scenario: 03 Load X amount of PPA messages
    Given I start the messaging service for the service bus topic "ffc-pay-request-dev"
    When I send 300 ppa messages using template "ppaFileMessage" to the service bus topic "ffc-pay-request-dev" with the batch number 91000
    Then I wait for 300 ppas to be processed for batch 91000